## 2. Root cause
agent_civilization/pipeline/dag.py::_run_stage waits with asyncio.wait_for(limit=min(timeout_s, remaining_plan_time)).
When the plan deadline is the smaller value, this inner wait can expire before _drive's outer asyncio.wait notices the deadline.
With STAGE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=1 the stage was then recorded as an ordinary stage timeout, run.deadline_hit stayed False, and the plan aggregate became 'failed' instead of 'timed_out'. Timing-dependent -> flaky on slow CI legs.

